# Dineros.cc — Overview

Dineros.cc is a predictive budgeting and financial management platform. It combines a Nuxt 4 frontend with server-side API routes (Nitro/H3), a MySQL 8 database accessed via Prisma, Redis-backed queues, and a companion microservice. The codebase is TypeScript-first and organized as a PNPM workspace with two packages: the main app and a microservice.

- Purpose: predictive budgeting, registers and entries, reoccurrences, reconciliation, reports, Plaid sync, crypto balances, savings goals, and more
- Tech stack (observed):
  - Nuxt 4 + Vue 3 (SSR/Nitro) and Pinia state
  - TypeScript, Vitest for unit/integration, Playwright for E2E
  - Prisma ORM (MySQL 8), prisma-field-encryption
  - Redis + BullMQ for queues
  - Plaid, Postmark, OpenAI clients
  - Dockerfiles + GKE manifests for deploy, GCR for images
- Audience: AI agents, maintainers, and contributors extending UI, API endpoints, business services, data model, and deployment scripts

## Packages (pnpm-workspace)

- app/ — Nuxt application, API (Nitro/H3), Prisma schema & migrations, services, queues, cron, tests
- microservice/ — companion service with its own Prisma schema subset and routes used for maintenance (e.g., encryption key migration)

## How to run locally (from repo root)

- Prereqs: Node >= 24.14.0, PNPM 10+, MySQL 8, Redis (see .nvmrc, README.md)
- Quick start:
  - cp .env.example .env
  - docker compose up -d (MySQL/Redis)
  - pnpm install
  - pnpm --filter dineros-app exec prisma migrate deploy
  - pnpm dev (serves on http://localhost:3000)

See README.md and AGENTS.md for environment caveats (e.g., overriding DATABASE_URL when a cloud agent injects production-like secrets).
